{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The quick-setting glue feels useful for small repairs because it complements the epoxy and adhesive tapes I already use.",
    "The metric screws and deburring wheel connect to my fastening, drilling, and metal-cutting work, provided their dimensions and equipment requirements fit my projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The long lag screws require a heavy wood-fastening job I do not currently have; buying other hardware does not create a need for that size.",
    "Decorative printer filament assumes access to a 3D printer, and the fishing magnet assumes an interest in salvage activities that my repair purchases do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My screw and bolt purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to offer many more fixed-size packs, even though I already own several assortments.",
    "A broad connection to tools and hands-on work seems to count too heavily when the item serves a different activity from my repairs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "For additional fasteners, I need the exact thread, length, head style, and material to fit a job and fill a gap in my existing supplies.",
    "Useful next purchases can complement what I already use, like quick-setting glue, while specialized supplies need evidence that I have the compatible equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my repair and fabrication interests but often mistake general relevance for an immediate need for particular supplies."
}"}
